Hi all,

This is to announce that sysstat 9.0.0 has been released and is 
available for download.

This version adds support for power management statistics. At the 
present time, only CPU frequency statistics are available.
This is the first version of the new, long-awaited, stable series!

Sysstat 9.0.0 is available for download from my web page at:
http://pagesperso-orange.fr/sebastien.godard/

280kB sysstat-9.0.0.tar.gz
228kB sysstat-9.0.0.tar.bz2
284kB sysstat-9.0.0-1.src.rpm
246kB sysstat-9.0.0-1.i586.rpm

It will also be available on ibiblio Linux archive site in a few days:
ftp://ibiblio.org/pub/Linux/system/status/

The sysstat utilities are a collection of performance monitoring tools 
for Linux. These include sar, sadf, mpstat, iostat, pidstat and sa 
tools. Check out http://pagesperso-orange.fr/sebastien.godard/features.html
to get a view of sysstat's main features.
Feedback always welcomed. Send your remarks and comments to:
sysstat <at> orange <dot> fr.

To learn some more about sysstat, check out
http://pagesperso-orange.fr/sebastien.godard/

Enjoy!

Changes vs 8.1.8 are:
* Option -m added to sar. This option is intended to display power 
management statistics. At the present time, only CPU frequency 
statistics are available.
* sadc updated: Option "-S POWER" tells sadc to collect power management 
statistics.
* sadf command updated to take into account power management statistics.
* [Mike Harvey]: No longer truncate the interval of time to 32 bits, as 
this may cause some problems when displaying average values statistics 
on machines with hundreds of CPU.
* Fixed a small bug in sar where it didn't parse arguments properly when 
some options were entered in a specific order.

